{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertices","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P8VerticesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A wrapper that adds a rule, such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"text":", can own any mutable directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representation as its base through this protocol and work on it without extra hashing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each vertex has a key: its index in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vertices.Index == Int"},{"type":"text","text":"). On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedPseudograph"},{"type":"text","text":") the key is the vertex’s slot, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":". On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" it is the vertex’s position, which never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes while the vertex exists and may leave holes. The underscored members read and write the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph by key, so a wrapper hashes a vertex once and then works on keys."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In addition to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"text":"’s laws:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_key(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.firstIndex(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_vertex(atKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is its inverse."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a vertex with key "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successors(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessors(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_outEdges(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_inEdges(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_outDegree(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_inDegree(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equal the unprefixed members for that vertex."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successorKeys(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the far ends’ keys, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_sourceKey(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_targetKey(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the endpoints’ keys."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertVertex(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" appends a vertex, which must not already be one, and returns its key,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.endIndex"},{"type":"text","text":" before the call. Keys of other vertices do not change."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inserts the edge and returns its position. On a simple graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), an edge already present is not inserted again and its position is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returned. Inserting an edge changes no key.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_removeVertex(atKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" removes the vertex and every edge at it. If the representation fills","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the hole by moving another vertex in (a swap-remove), it returns that vertex’s old key, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that vertex’s key becomes ","type":"text"},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Otherwise it returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and no other key changes.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeEdge(at:)"},{"type":"text","text":" removes the edge at a live position and returns it, and traps on any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position. Removing an edge changes no key."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(v)"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeVertex(atKey: _key(of: v)!)"},{"text":", returning the removed instance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_built(vertices:sourceKeys:targetKeys:reportingPositions:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_insertVertex(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for each vertex in order, then ","type":"text"},{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for each pair","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in order. It gives the same graph and the same position for each pair.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A wrapper may keep one table entry per 1024 keys, from the smallest live key to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.endIndex"},{"text":", plus O(1) per live vertex. That matches the representation’s own page","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"table. On a dense representation the keys are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"text":". On ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"text":" the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"span can exceed the vertex count, because removals leave holes and a decoded graph may start at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any position. Its decoder bounds the span at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"16 × vertexCount + 64"},{"text":" pages. Keys before the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smallest live key cost nothing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successorKeys(ofKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" return the stored rows typed as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuccessorIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PredecessorIndices"},{"type":"text","text":", whose elements here are keys. On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation keys and indices coincide. On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" the elements are positions,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which are vertex indices only while the graph has no holes. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successorIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then unavailable, but the key rows are not."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is not a requirement because its return type varies by representation."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":" returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(inserted:memberAfterInsert:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the multigraphs return the new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position, and a wrapper that rejects edges returns an optional. Generic code inserts an edge by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The underscored members are for wrappers inside the library. Callers use the representations’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own ","type":"text"},{"code":"insert","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"remove","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" members, which take vertices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"MutableDirectedGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph.swift#L54"},"title":"MutableDirectedGraph","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols015MutableDirectedA0P","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"],"type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(edge:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/remove(edge:)":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Removes one copy of ","type":"text"},{"code":"edge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". On a representation with parallel edges it removes the newest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copy. Never inserts or removes a vertex.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(edge:)","required":true,"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"remove"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"edge"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedEdgeV","text":"DirectedEdge"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedEdgeV","text":"DirectedEdge","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/remove(edge:)","title":"remove(edge:)"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)":{"title":"removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"removeAllEdges","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"keepingCapacity","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"required":true,"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/removealledges(keepingcapacity:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Removes every edge, keeping every vertex and its key."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/init()":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The empty graph."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()","required":true,"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/init()","title":"init()"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/remove(_:)":{"title":"remove(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"remove"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"required":true,"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/remove(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Removes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" and every edge at it."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods. In-adjacency usually costs extra"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage, so representations that store only out-adjacency conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" alone."}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)":{"title":"removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"removeAll","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"keepingCapacity","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"required":true,"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/removeall(keepingcapacity:)","abstract":[{"text":"Removes every vertex and edge.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertex":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","required":true,"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/vertex","title":"Vertex"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reserves space for at least "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" vertices and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":" edges."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)","required":true,"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"reserveCapacity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"vertexCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/reservecapacity(vertexcount:edgecount:)","title":"reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertices-swift.associatedtype":{"title":"Vertices","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertices","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Collection","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"required":true,"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/vertices-swift.associatedtype","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","title":"DirectedGraph","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","title":"MutableDirectedGraph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate."}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/insert(_:)":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Inserts "},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with no edges, if it is not already a vertex."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","required":true,"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"insert"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"text":") -> (inserted","kind":"text"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":", memberAfterInsert","kind":"text"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/insert(_:)","title":"insert(_:)"}}}